  "title": "Work item resolution: first issue wins instead of refusing ambiguity",
  "summary": "The work-item resolver no longer refuses a pull request whose visible text names more than one issue in its own repository. `own_issue` now returns the first candidate rather than the sole one, `find` drops the multi-issue refusal branch, and `check_binding` accepts a saved work item whenever the pull request text names that issue anywhere among the candidates. The `more_than_one_issue` reason string is deleted, and the four architecture/development documents that described the refusal are updated to describe first-wins precedence: the `Issue:` line wins, otherwise the first closing keyword does.",
